> randomly wrong (or I haven't found the pattern yet).
> 
> Is this a known problem? Or have I screwed something up?
> 

try setting the contents of the file /etc/sysconfig/clock   to:
CLOCKMODE="ARC"

this will use the ARC console clock... works for me on my UDB....

look for "clock" in /etc/rc.d/rc.sysinit    to see where the time gets set
when you boot your system.

