Subject: Re: moving linux from one disk to another

I have found that one of the following is quite fast and takes care of
problems that you will get into with cp:

for a whole disk copy (the fastest per data):

dump -0 -f - diskname | ( cd mountpt; restore -rf - )

For subdirectory to subdirectory:

find startdir -print | cpio -pad destdir

or

cd  startdir ; tar -cf - * | ( cd destdir; tar -xpf - )

